From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 11:15:59 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] drm/virtio: let the freezer freeze a task that waits for the
 host

A host that holds its virtio-gpu answers while the guest suspends keeps
every task that waits uninterruptibly for one from freezing, and the
suspend then fails with "tasks refusing to freeze". Sleep in a state the
freezer can freeze (virtio_gpu_wait_host_timeout(), which the creation
wait introduced) where the waiter holds no lock:

- the 5 s wait for a capset in the get-caps ioctl.

Mark a wait this way only where the task holds no lock, because a frozen
task keeps what it holds. The other uninterruptible waits stay as they
are, each with the lock its caller holds: the map-state waits in
virtio_gpu_vram_mmap() (mmap_lock) and in the dma-buf shm-region and
host-blob callbacks (the V4L2 device lock of the video driver that
calls them), the uuid wait (an importer may call it with its own locks
held), and the control and cursor queues' ring-full waits (the object
reservation and the DRM unplug SRCU). The probe-time and work-queue
waits are not user tasks, which the freezer leaves alone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_ioctl.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_ioctl.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_ioctl.c
index c2ad81b4543ebc18ab060aa4c27138cc7ea973ea..54955a5dd287d18b91dd98e11f5a5ab21156d040 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_ioctl.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/virtio/virtgpu_ioctl.c
@@ -477,8 +477,9 @@ static int virtio_gpu_get_caps_ioctl(struct drm_device *dev,
 	virtio_gpu_notify(vgdev);
 
 copy_exit:
-	ret = wait_event_timeout(vgdev->resp_wq,
-				 atomic_read(&cache_ent->is_valid), 5 * HZ);
+	ret = virtio_gpu_wait_host_timeout(vgdev->resp_wq,
+					   atomic_read(&cache_ent->is_valid),
+					   5 * HZ);
 	if (!ret)
 		return -EBUSY;
 
